<section image-layout="blank" id="zWyPZoJcSu"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="aFWW1SrX26" padding-top="32pt"><p role="eyebrow"><span text-color="#B83D34">Illustrated viewpoints—not real biographies</span></p><h2>The same years did not feel the same to everyone</h2><p font-size="lg"><b>People did not have equal rights or choices.</b></p><grid spacing="medium"><spacer span="2"></spacer><grid-item id="q6LQfu7ubs" colspan="14"><img style="--figure-radius: 999pt;" src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/gGD2C5OqPDa_aGW67kzph.png" saved-media-id="zfxsdimdmwxh2fq" source="image.ai-generated" width="160pt" image-style="southern-brazil-paper-museum" alt="Layered cut-paper and colored-pencil portrait of an illustrative free market seller named Rosa in 1830s–1840s southern Brazil, adult woman with medium-brown skin beside a simple produce basket and market cloth, historically grounded but non-specific clothing, restrained thoughtful expression, warm cream paper background, no text, no weapons" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1440,&quot;height&quot;:1440}"><h4>Rosa</h4><p font-size="16pt"><b>Free market seller</b></p><p font-size="16pt">She watches trade rules change.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="0L8QreX9N2" colspan="14"><img style="--figure-radius: 999pt;" src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/lgxSyDvqSpL5nmoDRcVvx.png" saved-media-id="j9wxj1llgjnq80i" source="image.ai-generated" width="160pt" image-style="southern-brazil-paper-museum" alt="Layered cut-paper and colored-pencil portrait of an illustrative rural worker named Tomás in 1830s–1840s southern Brazil, adult man with tan skin beside a travel bag and food sack, historically grounded but non-specific work clothing, calm serious expression, warm cream paper background, no text, no weapons" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1440,&quot;height&quot;:1440}"><h4>Tomás</h4><p font-size="16pt"><b>Rural worker</b></p><p font-size="16pt">Work, food, and travel shape his choices.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="fvvVFiQVdc" colspan="14"><img style="--figure-radius: 999pt;" src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/1g5c3NTv_hlHKIVrdYs4h.png" saved-media-id="faklibuhgmv1rgw" source="image.ai-generated" width="160pt" image-style="southern-brazil-paper-museum" alt="Layered cut-paper and colored-pencil portrait of an illustrative enslaved worker named Luzia in 1830s–1840s southern Brazil, adult Black woman standing with dignity beside folded cloth and a carrying basket, historically grounded but non-specific clothing, restrained direct expression, warm cream paper background, no chains, no violence, no text, no weapons" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1440,&quot;height&quot;:1440}"><h4>Luzia</h4><p font-size="16pt"><b>Enslaved worker</b></p><p font-size="16pt">She has far fewer rights. Slavery continues after the revolt.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Ln_Vcd2hoJ" colspan="14"><img style="--figure-radius: 999pt;" src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/Eso7Aks0Yke-EPaifM4xy.png" saved-media-id="ev5nhqxkrdhzxps" source="image.ai-generated" width="160pt" image-style="southern-brazil-paper-museum" alt="Layered cut-paper and colored-pencil portrait of an illustrative child named Davi in 1830s–1840s southern Brazil, brown-skinned child listening while nearby adult hands hold an opened letter with no readable writing, historically grounded but non-specific clothing, curious restrained expression, warm cream paper background, no text, no weapons" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1440,&quot;height&quot;:1440}"><h4>Davi</h4><p font-size="16pt"><b>Child</b></p><p font-size="16pt">Adults shape the news he hears.</p></grid-item><spacer span="2"></spacer></grid></grid-item></grid></section>